B.aqB=new A.eW("      Rotate [this] (in place) to a different orientation (any of the four 90-degree rotations).\n\n      This action does not involve moving to a different zone; the card stays in place and only changes its facing.\n      ",!0)
B.no=new A.dN("Reorient","Rotate [this] (in place) to a different orientation.",null,!1,null,0,"reorient")
B.aq8=new A.Zx()
B.np=new A.dN("Re-target","When this card is declared as a target; you can instead choose a different valid target for that effect.",null,!1,B.fe,9,"reTarget")
B.tJ=new A.dN("Transform",'When the transform condition is met, you must immediately resolve: "Sac [this]: you can summon from your [[Fables Deck]] a [Transformed] creature."',null,!1,B.a0,14,"transform")
B.aqp=s(["This action is only available for equipments.","See [[Equipment]] for a full explanation of this action."],t.s)
B.tK=new A.dN("Equip","Attach [this] to target creature.",null,!1,null,4,"equip")
B.aqD=new A.eW('      Target a creature zone (other than the one the attacking creature is in). Typically, a player will target their\n      opponent\'s zones for attacking.\n\n      Then, the Blocker (if any) must be determined; following these rules:\n\n      - If the targeted zone has a creature, that creature _must_ block the attack (except if it has [[Fading]]).\n\n      - If not, if the attacking creature has [[Evasive]], it cannot be blocked and this will be a direct attack.\n\n      - If not, if the controller of the zone has a creature that can target the zone, they can optionally select one\n        such creature to block the attack.\n\n      - If they chose not to or can\'t, the other player has a choice to block as well.\n\n      - If not, creature is attacking the controller of the zone directly.\n\n      **Note**: normally it is expected that each player only attack opponent zones, and similarly only block their own\n      zones; but the rules allow any interaction for full flexibility.\n\n      After the blocker (or lack thereof) is established, the **Strike Action** is added to the chain to be resolved.\n\n      For blocked attacks, both creatures deal [[Damage Counter | damage]] equal to their [[Might | Might Stat]] to each\n      other simultaneously. If at any point (as a state-based action) the damage counters on a creature equal or exceed\n      their [[Life | Life Stat]], they are destroyed.\n\n      However, during a [[Battle Event]], the attacking creature has **First Strike** against active blockers. This\n      means the attacker deals its damage first; if the active blocker is destroyed before it can deal damage back, the\n      attacker takes no damage. Passive blocks (where the creature in the targeted zone must block) are always\n      simultaneous as normal.\n\n      For direct attacks, regardless of the [[Might | Might Stat]] of the creature (as long as it is greater than 0), the\n      controller of the zone loses 1 [[HP]] and [[Draw | draws]] a card.\n\n      **Note**: Damage counters are **NOT** cleared at any step and stay forever!!!!!!!!!!!.\n\n      **Note**: Damage to creatures does **NOT** "pierce" (i.e. extra damage does not bleed to the player).\n\n      **Note**: a creature cannot attack or be blocked by itself, even if it is moved before the attack resolves. It\n      can however certain attack and block allied cards.\n\n      **Note**: creatures do not "tap"/"exhaust"/"exert" to attack or block as there is no tapping in [e:game].\n      However cards on the field can only perform one action per Event.\n\n      **Note**: while [[Summon | Summoning]] can typically only be done during the [[Deployment Phase]], there is no "summoning\n      sickness" in [e:game]. If via an effect such as [[Transform]] or [[Conscript]] a new creature is summoned during\n      an [[Event]], it _can_ perform one action during that event.\n\n      **Note**: blocking is _not_ an Action, but rather considered part of the [[Strike]] action itself.\n      ',!0)
B.k7=new A.dN("Strike","Target creature zone to fight with blocker or deal direct damage.",null,!1,null,2,"strike")
B.tL=new A.dN("Sidestep","Move a card to an empty adjacent zone (either conquered or unconquered), rotating to desired orientation.","Move to an empty adjacent zone.",!0,null,12,"sidestep")
B.aqG=new A.eW('      Target a different empty, conquered creature zone you control: move [this] to it, and then, optionally, rotate it\n      to a different orientation.\n\n      The destination zone must be a different zone from the one the creature is currently in, and must be targeted\n      beforehand, but the final rotation can be chosen at resolution.\n\n      A card can "jump over" other cards like a chess Knight to move; but it cannot move to an occupied zone.\n\n      Creatures with [[Explorer]] can target any (conquered or non-conquered) zones to move regardless of their arrows.\n      ',!0)
B.nq=new A.dN("March","Move to target empty, [[Conquered | conquered]] creature zone you control, rotating to desired orientation.",null,!1,null,1,"march")
B.aql=s([u.h,"The Creature Token must always be face-up (you can choose the orientation).","If the zone is no longer empty when this effect resolves: it fizzles."],t.s)
B.tM=new A.dN("Conscript","Summon a [[Creature Token]] to target empty conquered creature zone.",null,!1,null,5,"conscript")
B.aqy=s(["You _can_ switch them.","You _can_ re-organize face-down artifacts. This action does _not_ target."],t.s)
B.tN=new A.dN("Maneuver","Re-organize any number of connected artifacts you control into any number of your connected artifact zones you own.",null,!1,B.fe,7,"maneuver")
B.tO=new A.dN("Cleanse","Clear all conditions from a card.","Clear all conditions.",!0,null,13,"cleanse")
B.tP=new A.dN("Shift","Swap [this] with target card of the same type you control.",null,!1,null,11,"shift")
B.aqr=s(["Only when the zone [this] card is in is attacked. This effect is not relevant to Active Blocking.","If you choose to fade; the [Strike] becomes a direct attack and cannot be blocked by any other creature."],t.s)
B.ns=new A.dN("Fading","When [this] zone is targeted for a [Strike]: you can choose not to block.",null,!0,null,8,"fading")
B.a9U=new A.eW("      Wynn are purple, soft skinned elf-like people, taller and slimmer than humans, that live on the mountain-tops and\n      tunnels; adepts of elemental magic of primal power their spells come with an unsettling cost.\n\n      They inhabit the mountains and peaks to the east, at least until they become too cold and snowy to any survive.\n\n      The Wynn access their Fables Deck via deranged creature sacrifices, in which they attach the consumed cards\n      face-down to the summoned Fables to fuel their most powerful effects.\n      ",!0)
B.kh=new A.cb("Wynn","The Wynn",B.a9U,3,"wynn")
B.aqo=s(["[this] is not considered to have been summoned or flipped.",'Do not trigger "When summoned" or other "When flipped" effects for [this]',"Do not collect mana for the summon of [this].","Flip, summon and resolve any associated effects of the chosen replacement."],t.s)
